      "text": "Origin: New Guinea (~8000 BCE, earliest cultivation)\n  -> South Asia (India) by 400 BCE (\"reeds that give honey without bees\")\n  -> Arab expansion carries cane to Persia, then Mediterranean (700-1000 CE)\n  -> Crusaders encounter sugar in Holy Land -> European demand\n  -> Portuguese in Madeira and Sao Tome (1400s)\n  -> Columbus carries cane to Hispaniola on second voyage (1493)\n  -> Caribbean: ideal climate, slave labor -> sugar empire"
