        "title": "Rum and Sugarcane Spirits",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "MUCK PITS (Jamaican tradition):\n  Large pits of decomposing organic matter (animal bones, fruit waste, stillage)\n  Allowed to sit for years, developing complex microbial communities\n  Small quantities added to ferment -> extraordinary ester levels\n  Muck-pit traditions are associated especially with old Jamaican heavy-rum\n  marks; they are not universal across all Jamaican distilleries.\n  Secret: the specific microbial flora is part of a distillery's resource base"
    },
    {
